
Multivariable Linear Regression is used when you want to predict a 
target value using multiple independent features (input variables) 
instead of just one.

1.  What does it use?
Instead of using just one input:
Simple Linear Regression --> Salary = b_0 + b_1(Experience)


One feature → one prediction
You use several inputs:
Multivariable Linear Regression

Salary = b_0 +b_1(Experience)
            +b_2(Education)
            +b_3(Skills)
            +b_4(WorkingHours)

Multiple features → one prediction


2. What datasets should you use?
You need a dataset where one target column depends on multiple feature columns.Ex:

	        Features (X)	                      Target (y)
Experience, Education, Skills	                    Salary
Area, Bedrooms, Bathrooms, Location             	Price
Study Hours, Attendance, Previous Marks	            Final Score
Age, Mileage, Brand, Engine Size	                Price
Age, BMI, Children, Smoker	Insurance               Cost
TV, Radio, Newspaper spending	                    Sales
Income, Rent, Food, Transport	                    Savings

